lighter shade <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.T2.pic4" class="ltx_picture" height="8.04" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 8.98 8.04" width="8.98"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,8.04) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 1.94 L 0 6.11 C 0 7.18 0.87 8.04 1.94 8.04 L 7.04 8.04 C 8.11 8.04 8.98 7.18 8.98 6.11 L 8.98 1.94 C 8.98 0.87 8.11 0 7.04 0 L 1.94 0 C 0.87 0 0 0.87 0 1.94 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E5E5E5;" fill="#E5E5E5" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.55 1.94 L 0.55 6.11 C 0.55 6.87 1.17 7.49 1.94 7.49 L 7.04 7.49 C 7.81 7.49 8.43 6.87 8.43 6.11 L 8.43 1.94 C 8.43 1.17 7.81 0.55 7.04 0.55 L 1.94 0.55 C 1.17 0.55 0.55 1.17 0.55 1.94 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 4.49 4.02)"><foreignObject overflow="visible"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.T2.pic4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_phantom"><span style="visibility:hidden"></span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span> = range of moderate accuracies,
unshaded = range of low accuracies.
</span></figcaption>
