<div id="A6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We investigate how increasing the number of trainable parameters affects performance under BP, ZO and <span id="A6.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span>.
Tables <a href="#A6.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ F.4 Reducing Trainable Parameter Count ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and <a href="#A6.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ F.4 Reducing Trainable Parameter Count ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> present results across varying model sizes and <span id="A6.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LoRA</span> ranks, respectively.
Further comparison of convergence time is available in Figure <a href="#A6.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ F.4 Reducing Trainable Parameter Count ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In Table <a href="#A6.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ F.4 Reducing Trainable Parameter Count ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, we evaluate <span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BP-Checkpointing</span>, <span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ZO-Vanilla</span>, and <span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD-Vanilla</span> on OPT model variants of size 1.3B, 6.7B, and 13B.
As the model size increases, <span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BP-Checkpointing</span> consistently maintains high accuracy of <math id="A6.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>94%.
In contrast, ZO and <span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> exhibit noticeable drops in accuracy at larger model scales.
Notably, <span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> achieves 88.28% accuracy on the 1.3B model but declines to 77.07% on the 13B model, showing degradation from scaling the count of trainable parameters.
This result are consistent with our theoretical findings of convergence error bounded by the trainable parameter count (§<a href="#S3" title="3 Theoretical Analysis ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
Table <a href="#A6.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ F.4 Reducing Trainable Parameter Count ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> explores accuracy as a function of <span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LoRA</span> rank for OPT 6.7B.
While <span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BP-Checkpointing</span> degrades gracefully as rank increases (likely due to overfitting), <span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> becomes unstable and fails to converge beyond rank 1, yielding <span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">NaN</span> outputs for higher ranks.
<span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span>’s instability at higher <span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LoRA</span> ranks is due to inherent instability of perturbation-based gradient estimations, which we discuss in Appendix <a href="#A6.SS5" title="F.5 Failure Mode Analysis ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.5</span></a>.
ZO, while stable, shows limited improvement with increased rank, reaching only 68.97% accuracy at rank 32.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F7" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:39%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.21833v1/opt_13B_vanilla_runtime.svg" id="A6.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:191/132;" width="191" height="132"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F7.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A6.F7.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of convergence time among <span id="A6.F7.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BP-Checkpointing</span>, <span id="A6.F7.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD-Vanilla</span>, and <span id="A6.F7.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ZO-Vanilla</span> with OPT(13B) on AGNews dataset.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.5 </span>Failure Mode Analysis</h3>

<div id="A6.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to understand why variance reduction methods or adaptive optimizers sometimes fail to make <span id="A6.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> and ZO converge, or converge at a suboptimal accuracy; we present failure mode analysis with different optimizers and SVRG.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.5.1 </span>Challenges with Optimizer Choice</h4>

<div id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we discuss a distinct failure mode of <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> which has been frequently observed in our preliminary experiments:
the computed Jacobian-vector products (<span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span>) abruptly spike in magnitude.
These sudden surges lead to disproportionately large gradient updates, destabilizing training and hindering convergence.
A similar failure mode has been observed in zero-order (ZO) methods, where the projected gradients, mathematically equivalent to <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span>’s <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> values, exhibit comparable instability.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A6.F9.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_bottom" style="width:120.8pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.21833v1/unstable_jvp_optimizer.svg" id="A6.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:167/119;" width="167" height="119"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F9.fig1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A6.F9.fig1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Effect of <span id="A6.F9.fig1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AdamW</span> and <span id="A6.F9.fig1.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SGD</span> optimizers on <span id="A6.F9.fig1.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> values in <span id="A6.F9.fig1.6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> on GSM8K dataset.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A6.F9.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_bottom" style="width:213.9pt;">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A6.F9.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.21833v1/unstable_gradients_adamw.svg" id="A6.F9.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:295/214;" width="295" height="214"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F9.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A6.F9.sf1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">AdamW<span id="A6.F9.sf1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> optimizer.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A6.F9.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.21833v1/stable_gradients_sgd.svg" id="A6.F9.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:295/209;" width="295" height="209"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F9.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A6.F9.sf2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">SGD<span id="A6.F9.sf2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> optimizer.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F9.fig2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A6.F9.fig2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mean of effective gradients of Backpropagation and Forward-mode AD with <span id="A6.F9.fig2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AdamW</span> and SGD optimizers on GSM8K dataset.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A6.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ F.5.1 Challenges with Optimizer Choice ‣ F.5 Failure Mode Analysis ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> illustrates the impact of optimizer choice, specifically <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AdamW</span> (adaptive) versus <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SGD</span> (non-adaptive), on <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> values in <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span>.
Under <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SGD</span>, <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> values remain bounded within a stable range of <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-50,50]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-50,50]</annotation></semantics></math> for the case of GSM8K dataset.
However, with <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AdamW</span>, these values exhibit a gradual increase followed by sharp spikes for certain datasets including GSM8K.
In some cases, the spikes reach 8–10<math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> higher magnitudes than the stable baseline observed with <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SGD</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A6.F9.sf1" title="In Figure 9 ‣ F.5.1 Challenges with Optimizer Choice ‣ F.5 Failure Mode Analysis ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9(a)</span></a> and <a href="#A6.F9.sf2" title="In Figure 9 ‣ F.5.1 Challenges with Optimizer Choice ‣ F.5 Failure Mode Analysis ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9(b)</span></a> further illustrate the implications of these spikes.
Under <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AdamW</span>, the effective gradient magnitudes produced by <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> exhibit substantially higher variance than those from backpropagation, indicating instability and less reliable gradient directions.
These inflated updates also increase weight magnitudes, which in turn amplify subsequent <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> evaluations, since these depend on both the current weights and their perturbations.
This positive feedback loop can lead to divergence and, eventually, <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">NaN</span> values in <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> computations, as observed in several <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> runs in Table <a href="#A6.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ F.4 Reducing Trainable Parameter Count ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.
Even when divergence does not occur, the resulting gradient updates can be excessively noisy or of high magnitude, leading to suboptimal convergence.
In contrast, under <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SGD</span>, the effective gradients computed by <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> closely mirror those from backpropagation across most iterations, with stable behavior and no evidence of runaway magnitudes.
We posit that this cascading rise in magnitude for the case of <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AdamW</span> is due to its adaptive nature, where a rolling average of historical and current gradients is computed each iteration, leading to amplification of higher magnitude gradients.
In contrast, the impact of <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> spikes is diminished with non-adaptive SGD since the previous iteration’s gradients would have limited effect (to only one iteration’s gradient updates).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This stark contrast highlights a critical interaction between optimizer choice and the numerical stability of <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span>.
While <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AdamW</span> is widely favored for its adaptive learning rates and regularization capabilities, its use with <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> (and by extension ZO) can introduce harmful gradient artifacts which are driven by uncontrolled <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> amplification.
These results underscore the specific vulnerabilities in gradient estimation methods and point to a need for further study into stabilizing <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> and ZO for more reliable deployment in large-scale training regimes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.5.2 </span>Challenges with SVRG</h4>

<div id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we discuss a failure mode of SVRG observed in the context of text generation tasks.
While SVRG improves performance for both <span id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ZO-Vanilla</span> and <span id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FwAD-Vanilla</span> baselines by 4.04–11.13 and 1.97–3.86, respectively, in many settings, it leads to performance degradation in certain sequence modeling tasks like GSM8K.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F10" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A6.F10.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.21833v1/svrg_fmad_jvp.svg" id="A6.F10.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/368;" width="476" height="368"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F10.sf1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A6.F10.sf1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The current iteration’s <span id="A6.F10.sf1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span>, <span id="A6.F10.sf1.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> computed based on the snapshot weights, and the difference between these two values.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A6.F10.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.21833v1/svrg_fmad_gradients.svg" id="A6.F10.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/386;" width="476" height="386"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F10.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A6.F10.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Magnitude of the mean effective full gradients (computed at specific epoch intervals) and the current iteration’s mini-batch gradient.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="A6.F10.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Impact of incorporating SVRG into <span id="A6.F10.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> on (a) <span id="A6.F10.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> values and the mean of effective full-batch and (b) mini-batch gradients, evaluated on the GSM8K dataset.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A6.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ F.5.2 Challenges with SVRG ‣ F.5 Failure Mode Analysis ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> illustrates the behavior of <span id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> values and the corresponding gradients when SVRG is applied to <span id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> on the GSM8K dataset.
In Figure <a href="#A6.F10.sf1" title="In Figure 10 ‣ F.5.2 Challenges with SVRG ‣ F.5 Failure Mode Analysis ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10(a)</span></a>, we observe that the difference between the <span id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> computed on the current model weights and the one computed on the snapshot weights is minimal.
Consequently, the control variate, the difference between mini-batch gradients at current and snapshot weights, has little impact relative to the magnitude of the full gradient.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This hypothesis is supported by Figure <a href="#A6.F10.sf2" title="In Figure 10 ‣ F.5.2 Challenges with SVRG ‣ F.5 Failure Mode Analysis ‣ Appendix F Additional Results ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10(b)</span></a>, which shows that the mean of the effective full gradients remains consistently large, while the mini-batch gradient magnitudes are significantly smaller.
Because the full gradients are updated only at periodic intervals (every 5 epochs in our case), their inflated magnitude dominates the update direction across multiple steps.
This inflation stems from the accumulation of large <span id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> values during the summation of per-batch gradients, occasionally resulting in outlier gradients with extremely high norms.
As a result, the SVRG mechanism fails to provide meaningful variance reduction and instead perpetuates overly large updates, ultimately degrading model performance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">A similar performance degradation was observed in <span id="A6.SS5.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ZO-SVRG</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>, albeit on a smaller model with approximately 852K parameters.
However, that work does not address the scalability challenges of SVRG-based methods in the context of zeroth-order optimization.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Signal Propagation for Gradient Computation</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A key difference between BP and <span id="A7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span>/ZO methods lies in how they propagate the loss signal to compute weight updates.
BP computes the derivative of the loss <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to each weight <math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, effectively mapping changes in the loss to precise updates in the parameter space.
The gradients of the intermediate activations, computed during the backward pass, are also derived from <math id="A7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, allowing the loss signal to guide every stage of the update.
This direct path from the loss to the parameters makes BP a <span id="A7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">loss-to-weights</span> approach, where the signal flows backward through the network in a structured and deterministic way.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, both <span id="A7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> and ZO adopt a <span id="A7.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">weights-to-loss</span> perspective:
they estimate how perturbations in the weights, <math id="A7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\boldsymbol{w}=\boldsymbol{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒘</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\boldsymbol{w}=\boldsymbol{v}</annotation></semantics></math>; affect the loss, <math id="A7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The forward-mode Jacobian-vector product (<span id="A7.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span>) and the ZO projected gradient scalar both incorporate the resulting change in the loss, but they do so indirectly.
Specifically, they multiply <math id="A7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> by the perturbation direction <math id="A7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}</annotation></semantics></math> to approximate weight gradients (as detailed in Equations <a href="#S3.E4" title="In Theorem 3.2 (Error Bound for Zero-Order Optimization). ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#S3.E6" title="In Theorem 3.3 (Error Bound for Forward-Mode AD). ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
However, in these approaches, the intermediate changes <math id="A7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta y_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta y_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> (which influence <math id="A7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>) are driven by the initial perturbations <math id="A7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta w_{p}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta w_{p}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>; not by the loss.
As a result, the variance introduced at the input level through the perturbations propagates forward through the network, ultimately contaminating the gradient signal.
This lack of an explicit loss-driven mechanism for shaping activation gradients leads to noisier gradient updates.
Consequently, <span id="A7.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> and ZO require stricter step size constraints (see Theorems <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (Error Bound for Zero-Order Optimization). ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3 (Error Bound for Forward-Mode AD). ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>) and exhibit degraded convergence behavior.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, both <span id="A7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> and ZO optimization methods incur additional noise and estimation error compared to backpropagation.
This noise is not just a side effect, it is an inherent consequence of using random perturbations to estimate gradients.
In both <span id="A7.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> and ZO, the injection of perturbations <math id="A7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\boldsymbol{w}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒘</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\boldsymbol{w}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> is core to the algorithmic process, and the resulting activation (<math id="A7.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) and loss variations (<math id="A7.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>) carry this randomness forward.
Therefore, the gradient estimates vary depending on the sampled perturbation, making noise a deterministic outcome of the method itself.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In essence, while BP precisely channels loss information to guide weight updates, <span id="A7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FmAD</span> and ZO rely on stochastic approximations that make their updates fundamentally noisy and less targeted.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Computational Complexity</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we analyze the computational complexity of different methods used to compute gradients in a neural network setting.
We begin with a one-layer neural network, providing a detailed breakdown of the computational cost for the forward pass, backpropagation, zero-order optimization, and forward-mode automatic differentiation.
Understanding these complexities is essential for evaluating the efficiency of gradient computation methods, especially in resource-constrained environments.
Empirical computational cost of the gradient computation methods is shown in §<a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5 Comparison on Computation Cost ‣ 4 Empirical Evaluation ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.1 </span>Basics</h3>

<div id="A8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we analyze the computational complexity of a one-layer neural network <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> with weight matrix <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The network takes an input <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and produces an output <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
While we focus on a single-layer setting for clarity, the analysis naturally extends to a deep neural network with <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers, each with weight matrix <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A8.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Forward Pass.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since all three gradient computation methods share the same forward pass, we first establish its computational complexity.
The forward pass consists of a matrix multiplication <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=xw" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=xw</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> has dimensions <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> has dimensions <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times m</annotation></semantics></math>.
This results in a computational complexity of <math id="A8.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(dm)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(dm)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.2 </span>Backpropagation</h3>

<div id="A8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Backpropagation requires computing the gradient of the loss <math id="A8.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the weights, given by</p>
<table id="A8.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial y}\cdot\frac{\partial y}{\partial w}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial y}\cdot\frac{\partial y}{\partial w}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The first term, <math id="A8.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial y}</annotation></semantics></math>, involves differentiating the loss with respect to the output, which has a computational complexity of <math id="A8.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The second term, <math id="A8.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial y}{\partial w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial y}{\partial w}</annotation></semantics></math>, follows from the linear transformation <math id="A8.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=xw" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=xw</annotation></semantics></math>, contributing a complexity of <math id="A8.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(dm)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(dm)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The final gradient computation involves the multiplication of a <math id="A8.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times m</annotation></semantics></math> matrix with an <math id="A8.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times d</annotation></semantics></math> matrix, resulting in an additional complexity of <math id="A8.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(dm)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(dm)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Although activation functions introduce constant factors, 3 for the last layer and 5 for intermediate layers, these constants do not affect the asymptotic complexity. Hence, the overall computational complexity of backpropagation remains <math id="A8.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(dm)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(dm)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.3 </span>Zero-Order Optimization</h3>

<div id="A8.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The zero-order optimization method with central finite differences involves perturbing the weights twice, evaluating at <math id="A8.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\boldsymbol{w}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})\text{ and }(\boldsymbol{w}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\boldsymbol{w}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})\text{ and }(\boldsymbol{w}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}),</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="A8.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math> is a randomly sampled perturbation and <math id="A8.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a small step size.
The element-wise multiplication <math id="A8.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}</annotation></semantics></math> incurs a computational cost of <math id="A8.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(dm)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(dm)</annotation></semantics></math>, as does the addition and subtraction with <math id="A8.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since each perturbation requires evaluating the function at the perturbed points, the function evaluations <math id="A8.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\boldsymbol{w}\pm\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>±</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\boldsymbol{w}\pm\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})</annotation></semantics></math> also contribute a complexity of <math id="A8.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(dm)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(dm)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A8.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> such perturbations per iteration, the total computational cost sums to <math id="A8.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(ndm)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(ndm)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A8.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of perturbations used in each iteration.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Compared to the forward pass on the original weights <math id="A8.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, zero-order adds a constant of 4, which gets absorbed in <math id="A8.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(ndm)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(ndm)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.4 </span>Forward-Mode AD</h3>

<div id="A8.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A8.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> (Jacobian-vector product) computation incurs a complexity of <math id="A8.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(dm)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(dm)</annotation></semantics></math>, as it partially computes <math id="A8.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The resulting <span id="A8.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jvp</span> is then multiplied with the perturbation vector <math id="A8.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the weight gradient for <math id="A8.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A8.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}</annotation></semantics></math> has dimensions <math id="A8.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times m</annotation></semantics></math>, this multiplication also has a computational complexity of <math id="A8.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(dm)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(dm)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Repeating this process <math id="A8.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> times for <math id="A8.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> perturbations per iteration leads to a total computational cost of <math id="A8.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(ndm)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(ndm)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Proofs of Convergence Bounds</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section includes the details on upper error bounds of all three gradient computation methods:
Backpropagation,
Zero-order optimization,
and Forward-mode Auto Differentiation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A9.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.1 </span>Basics</h3>

<div id="A9.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All examples of gradient computation methods are based on a function <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, which, in the context of machine learning, corresponds to a neural network.
This function <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is composed of nested functions <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[p]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[p]</annotation></semantics></math>; where each function corresponds to an intermediate output (or activation) <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}=f_{i}(w_{i},y_{i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}=f_{i}(w_{i},y_{i-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, generated from the input weights <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and previous activation <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="A9.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is set to <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be data points in ML.
We assume that <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, for the ease of exposition.
The input weights are represented by the vector <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{w}={w_{1},w_{2},\dots,w_{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{w}={w_{1},w_{2},\dots,w_{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{[1,\dots,p]}\in\mathbb{R}^{[m_{1},\dots,m_{p}]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{[1,\dots,p]}\in\mathbb{R}^{[m_{1},\dots,m_{p}]}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The intermediate outputs, or activations, are denoted by <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{y}={y_{1},\dots,y_{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{y}={y_{1},\dots,y_{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The final output is <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=y_{p}=f(\boldsymbol{w},x)\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=y_{p}=f(\boldsymbol{w},x)\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, where typically <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&lt;&lt;m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&lt;&lt;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&lt;&lt;m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[p]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[p]</annotation></semantics></math>.
The loss function <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(y,\hat{y})\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(y,\hat{y})\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is then computed to measure the difference between the predicted output <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and the true target values <math id="A9.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">With gradient descent, one update to the weights <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{w}</annotation></semantics></math> looks like this,</p>
<table id="A9.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}\leftarrow\boldsymbol{w}_{t}-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}\leftarrow\boldsymbol{w}_{t}-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the iteration count, and <math id="A9.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is the learning rate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The objective is to minimize <math id="A9.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A9.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\boldsymbol{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\boldsymbol{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition I.1</span></span><span id="A9.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Optimality Gap)<span id="A9.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The optimality gap at iteration <math id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the difference between the function value at the current iterate <math id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the function value at an optimal solution <math id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{w}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{w}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A9.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{t}=f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-f(\boldsymbol{w}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{t}=f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-f(\boldsymbol{w}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The optimality gap quantifies how far the current function value is from the optimal value.
In convergence analysis, the goal is to show that this gap decreases over iterations.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.2 </span>Assumptions</h3>

<div id="A9.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption I.2</span></span><span id="A9.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smoothness)<span id="A9.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A9.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A9.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, meaning that its gradient is Lipschitz continuous with constant <math id="A9.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
That is, for all <math id="A9.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{w},\boldsymbol{w}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{w},\boldsymbol{w}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the function <math id="A9.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies,</p>
<table id="A9.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}^{\prime})-\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||\leq L||\boldsymbol{w}^{\prime}-\boldsymbol{w}||." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}^{\prime})-\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||\leq L||\boldsymbol{w}^{\prime}-\boldsymbol{w}||.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.3 </span>Lemmas</h3>

<div id="A9.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma I.3</span></span><span id="A9.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bias of Gradient Estimate of the Central Finite Difference)<span id="A9.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A9.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\boldsymbol{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\boldsymbol{v})</annotation></semantics></math> be the gradient estimate obtained using the central finite difference method with a perturbation vector <math id="A9.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the expectation of the estimator satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">implying that the central finite difference gradient estimator is unbiased up to first-order error terms.
Furthermore, the second moment of the estimator satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|g(\boldsymbol{v})\|^{2}\right]=\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+2)+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|g(\boldsymbol{v})\|^{2}\right]=\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+2)+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A9.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start with one evaluation of the central finite difference, for a perturbation <math id="A9.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. The full derivation is given in Theorem <a href="#A9.Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem I.8 (Error Bound of Zero-Order Optimization). ‣ I.4 Theorems ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.8</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle g(\boldsymbol{v})=\left((\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)\boldsymbol{v}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g(\boldsymbol{v})=\left((\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)\boldsymbol{v}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">In order to measure the bias of the above gradient estimate, we take expectation with respect to the randomness of <math id="A9.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[g(\boldsymbol{v})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[g(\boldsymbol{v})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)\boldsymbol{v}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)\boldsymbol{v}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\boldsymbol{v}\right]+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\boldsymbol{v}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\boldsymbol{v}\right]+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\boldsymbol{v}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})I_{d}+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)\cdot 0\quad\text{(since $\boldsymbol{v}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})$)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mtext>(since </mtext><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})I_{d}+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)\cdot 0\quad\text{(since $\boldsymbol{v}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})$)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\therefore\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[g(\boldsymbol{v})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∴</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\therefore\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[g(\boldsymbol{v})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">This shows that the estimator is unbiased.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we analyze the second moment of the estimator:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|g(\boldsymbol{v})\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|g(\boldsymbol{v})\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E18.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\left\|(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)\boldsymbol{v}\right\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\left\|(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)\boldsymbol{v}\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))^{2}\|\boldsymbol{v}\|^{2}\right]+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|\boldsymbol{v}\|^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))^{2}\|\boldsymbol{v}\|^{2}\right]+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|\boldsymbol{v}\|^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the known expectation property of Gaussian vectors:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\boldsymbol{v}\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\|\boldsymbol{v}\|^{2}\right]=(d+2)I_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\boldsymbol{v}\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\|\boldsymbol{v}\|^{2}\right]=(d+2)I_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|g(\boldsymbol{v})\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|g(\boldsymbol{v})\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E21.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\text{Tr}((\boldsymbol{v}\boldsymbol{v}^{\top})\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top}\boldsymbol{v}\boldsymbol{v}^{\top})\right]+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝒗</mi><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\text{Tr}((\boldsymbol{v}\boldsymbol{v}^{\top})\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top}\boldsymbol{v}\boldsymbol{v}^{\top})\right]+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Tr}(\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top})(d+2)+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Tr}(\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top})(d+2)+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+2)+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+2)+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma I.4</span></span><span id="A9.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Variance of Gradient Estimate of the Central Finite Difference)<span id="A9.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{v})</annotation></semantics></math> be the central finite difference gradient estimator using <math id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> perturbations <math id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}_{1},\dots,\boldsymbol{v}_{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}_{1},\dots,\boldsymbol{v}_{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, given by</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i}),\quad\text{where}\quad g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})=\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})-f(\boldsymbol{w}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})}{2\epsilon}\boldsymbol{v}_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i}),\quad\text{where}\quad g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})=\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})-f(\boldsymbol{w}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})}{2\epsilon}\boldsymbol{v}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assuming the finite-difference step <math id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, the variance of the estimator satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\frac{1}{n}\left(\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+1)+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\frac{1}{n}\left(\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+1)+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This result shows that the variance of the gradient estimator scales as <math id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}((d+1)/n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((d+1)/n)</annotation></semantics></math>, which quantifies how the dimension <math id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of samples <math id="A9.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> influence the estimator’s variance.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A9.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can derive the variance of the estimator</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})\text{, with }g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})=\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})-f(\boldsymbol{w}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})}{2\epsilon}\boldsymbol{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>, with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})\text{, with }g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})=\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})-f(\boldsymbol{w}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})}{2\epsilon}\boldsymbol{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">by computing</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]-||\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]||^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]-||\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]||^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">For clarity, in the following we assume that the finite-difference step is chosen so that the bias is negligible (i.e. the estimator is unbiased according to Lemma <a href="#A9.EGx12" title="Lemma I.3 (Bias of Gradient Estimate of the Central Finite Difference). ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.3</span></a>, so that <math id="A9.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math>. (We can add the higher-order remainder later.)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We write the second moment (squared norm) of <math id="A9.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\left|\left|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})\right|\right|^{2}\right]=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})^{\top}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\left|\left|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})\right|\right|^{2}\right]=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})^{\top}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We split the sum into diagonal and off-diagonal parts:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})||^{2}]+\sum_{i\neq j}\mathbb{E}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})^{\top}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})||^{2}]+\sum_{i\neq j}\mathbb{E}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})^{\top}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since the <math id="A9.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})^{\top}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})^{\top}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E29.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})]^{\top}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})]^{\top}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{for }i\neq j." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{for }i\neq j.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}(n\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v})||^{2}]+n(n-1)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}(n\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v})||^{2}]+n(n-1)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging the above result, along with the result derived from Lemma <a href="#A9.EGx12" title="Lemma I.3 (Bias of Gradient Estimate of the Central Finite Difference). ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.3</span></a> on <math id="A9.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]||^{2}=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]||^{2}=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, in Equation <a href="#A9.E26" title="In Proof. ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\left(n\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v})||^{2}]+n(n-1)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}\right)-||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\left(n\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v})||^{2}]+n(n-1)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}\right)-||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v})||^{2}]-||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v})||^{2}]-||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">The second moment of the estimator was derived in Lemma <a href="#A9.EGx12" title="Lemma I.3 (Bias of Gradient Estimate of the Central Finite Difference). ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.3</span></a>, in Equation <a href="#A9.E23" title="In Proof. ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>.
We use that result in the above equation as follows,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+2)+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d-\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+2)+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d-\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+1)+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+1)+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">This leads us to a variance bound that scales as <math id="A9.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d+1}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d+1}{n}</annotation></semantics></math> times <math id="A9.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\nabla f(\theta)||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\nabla f(\theta)||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (plus a <math id="A9.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> contribution), which exhibits the dependence of variance of the estimator <math id="A9.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math> on the dimension <math id="A9.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of samples <math id="A9.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A9.SS3.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="122.88" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 122.88" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,122.88) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 116.98 C 0 120.24 2.64 122.88 5.91 122.88 L 471.47 122.88 C 474.73 122.88 477.38 120.24 477.38 116.98 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 116.98 C 1.97 119.15 3.73 120.91 5.91 120.91 L 471.47 120.91 C 473.65 120.91 475.41 119.15 475.41 116.98 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:6.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="95.32" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 92.63)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A9.SS3.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A9.SS3.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The key difference between the above two lemmas and the next two lemmas is that the central finite difference estimator introduces a small <math id="A9.SS3.p5.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> bias due to numerical approximation, whereas the forward-mode AD estimator is exactly unbiased.
Additionally, the second moment of the central finite difference estimator includes an extra <math id="A9.SS3.p5.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\epsilon^{2})d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϵ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\epsilon^{2})d</annotation></semantics></math> term, which is absent in forward-mode AD, making the latter more precise.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma I.5</span></span><span id="A9.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bias of Gradient Estimate of Forward-mode Auto Differentiation)<span id="A9.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A9.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\boldsymbol{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\boldsymbol{v})</annotation></semantics></math> be the gradient estimate obtained using the central finite difference method with a perturbation vector <math id="A9.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, the expectation of the estimator satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">implying that the central finite difference gradient estimator is unbiased.
Furthermore, the second moment of the estimator satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|g(\boldsymbol{v})\|^{2}\right]=\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+2)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|g(\boldsymbol{v})\|^{2}\right]=\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A9.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start with one evaluation of forward-mode auto differentiation, for a perturbation <math id="A9.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The full derivation is given in Theorem <a href="#A9.Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem I.9 (Error Bound of Forward-mode Auto Differentiation). ‣ Back to Equation , plugging in Term1 and Term2: ‣ I.4 Theorems ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.9</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle g(\boldsymbol{v})=\left(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\right)\boldsymbol{v}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g(\boldsymbol{v})=\left(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\right)\boldsymbol{v}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">In order to measure the bias of the above gradient estimate, we take expectation with respect to the randomness of <math id="A9.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[g(\boldsymbol{v})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[g(\boldsymbol{v})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E38.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\boldsymbol{v}\right]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\boldsymbol{v}\right]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\therefore\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[g(\boldsymbol{v})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∴</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\therefore\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[g(\boldsymbol{v})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">This shows that the estimator is unbiased.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we analyze the second moment of the estimator:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|g(\boldsymbol{v})\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|g(\boldsymbol{v})\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E41.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\left\|(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}\right\|^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))^{2}\|\boldsymbol{v}\|^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\left\|(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}\right\|^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[(\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))^{2}\|\boldsymbol{v}\|^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the known expectation property of Gaussian vectors:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\boldsymbol{v}\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\|\boldsymbol{v}\|^{2}\right]=(d+2)I_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\boldsymbol{v}\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\|\boldsymbol{v}\|^{2}\right]=(d+2)I_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">We obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|g(\boldsymbol{v})\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\|g(\boldsymbol{v})\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E43.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\text{Tr}((\boldsymbol{v}\boldsymbol{v}^{\top})\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top}\boldsymbol{v}\boldsymbol{v}^{\top})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝒗</mi><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\text{Tr}((\boldsymbol{v}\boldsymbol{v}^{\top})\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top}\boldsymbol{v}\boldsymbol{v}^{\top})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Tr}(\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top})(d+2)=\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+2)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Tr}(\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top})(d+2)=\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma I.6</span></span><span id="A9.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Variance of Gradient Estimate of Forward-mode Auto Differentiation)<span id="A9.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{v})</annotation></semantics></math> be the central finite difference gradient estimator using <math id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> perturbations <math id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}_{1},\dots,\boldsymbol{v}_{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}_{1},\dots,\boldsymbol{v}_{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, given by</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i}),\quad\text{where}\quad g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})=(\boldsymbol{v}_{i}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i}),\quad\text{where}\quad g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})=(\boldsymbol{v}_{i}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assuming the finite-difference step <math id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, the variance of the estimator satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\frac{1}{n}\left(\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+1)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\frac{1}{n}\left(\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+1)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This result shows that the variance of the gradient estimator scales as <math id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}((d+1)/n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((d+1)/n)</annotation></semantics></math>, which quantifies how the dimension <math id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of samples <math id="A9.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> influence the estimator’s variance.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A9.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can derive the variance of the estimator</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})\text{, with }g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})=(\boldsymbol{v}_{i}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>, with </mtext><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})\text{, with }g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})=(\boldsymbol{v}_{i}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">by computing</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]-||\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]||^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]-||\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]||^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">The estimator is unbiased according to Lemma <a href="#A9.EGx29" title="Lemma I.5 (Bias of Gradient Estimate of Forward-mode Auto Differentiation). ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.5</span></a>, so that <math id="A9.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We write the second moment (squared norm) of <math id="A9.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\left|\left|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})\right|\right|^{2}\right]=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})^{\top}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\left|\left|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})\right|\right|^{2}\right]=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})^{\top}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">We split the sum into diagonal and off-diagonal parts:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})||^{2}]+\sum_{i\neq j}\mathbb{E}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})^{\top}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})||^{2}]+\sum_{i\neq j}\mathbb{E}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})^{\top}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since the <math id="A9.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})^{\top}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})^{\top}g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E50.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})]^{\top}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})]^{\top}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[g(\boldsymbol{v}_{j})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E50.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{for }i\neq j." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{for }i\neq j.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}(n\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v})||^{2}]+n(n-1)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}(n\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v})||^{2}]+n(n-1)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging the above result, along with the result derived from Lemma <a href="#A9.EGx12" title="Lemma I.3 (Bias of Gradient Estimate of the Central Finite Difference). ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.3</span></a> on <math id="A9.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]||^{2}=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]||^{2}=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, in Equation <a href="#A9.E47" title="In Proof. ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\left(n\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v})||^{2}]+n(n-1)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}\right)-||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\left(n\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v})||^{2}]+n(n-1)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}\right)-||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v})||^{2}]-||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||g(\boldsymbol{v})||^{2}]-||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p9.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p9.6.1" class="ltx_text">The second moment of the estimator was derived in Lemma <a href="#A9.EGx29" title="Lemma I.5 (Bias of Gradient Estimate of Forward-mode Auto Differentiation). ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.5</span></a>, in Equation <a href="#A9.E44" title="In Proof. ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>.
We use that result in the above equation as follows,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+2)-\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+2)-\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+1)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\left(\|\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})\|^{2}(d+1)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS3.p9.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS3.p9.7.1" class="ltx_text">This leads us to a variance bound that scales as <math id="A9.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d+1}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d+1}{n}</annotation></semantics></math> times <math id="A9.SS3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\nabla f(\theta)||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\nabla f(\theta)||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which exhibits the dependence of variance of the estimator <math id="A9.SS3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math> on the dimension <math id="A9.SS3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of samples <math id="A9.SS3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.4 </span>Theorems</h3>

<div id="A9.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The given analysis for all gradient computation methods is for <span id="A9.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">a non-convex objective</span> <math id="A9.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">We begin by reiterating the descent lemma applied to gradients computed by backpropagation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem I.7</span></span><span id="A9.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Error Bound of Backpropagation)<span id="A9.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a differentiable, <math id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth
function.
Consider the gradient descent update rule:</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}=\boldsymbol{w}_{t}-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}=\boldsymbol{w}_{t}-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is the step size (learning rate).
Suppose <math id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leq\frac{1}{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leq\frac{1}{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, after <math id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> iterations, the minimum gradient norm satisfies the following bound:</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{t\in[T]}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}\leq\frac{2L}{T}\left(f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{t\in[T]}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}\leq\frac{2L}{T}\left(f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This bound shows that gradient descent achieves an <math id="A9.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\frac{1}{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\frac{1}{T})</annotation></semantics></math> convergence rate in terms of gradient norm, which is the optimal rate for first-order methods in smooth
optimization.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A9.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using Assumption <a href="#A9.EGx10" title="Assumption I.2 (Smoothness). ‣ I.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.2</span></a>,
we apply the smoothness condition, which gives the following quadratic upper bound:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E56.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L}{2}||\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{w}_{t}||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L}{2}||\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{w}_{t}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting the gradient descent update rule Equation <a href="#A9.E8" title="In I.1 Basics ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, we obtain,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\therefore f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}+\frac{L}{2}\eta^{2}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∴</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\therefore f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}+\frac{L}{2}\eta^{2}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging the above terms,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\therefore f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})\leq-\eta||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}=-\left(\eta-\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\right)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∴</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\therefore f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})\leq-\eta||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}=-\left(\eta-\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\right)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">To ensure progress in minimizing <math id="A9.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math>, we need the term <math id="A9.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\frac{L\eta}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\frac{L\eta}{2})</annotation></semantics></math> to be positive.
Hence we assume <math id="A9.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq\frac{1}{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq\frac{1}{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, along with <math id="A9.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\therefore f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})\leq-\frac{1}{2L}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∴</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\therefore f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})\leq-\frac{1}{2L}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Summing over <math id="A9.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A9.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E60.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left(f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})\right)\leq-\frac{1}{2L}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left(f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})\right)\leq-\frac{1}{2L}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">The left-hand side forms a telescoping sum, resulting in</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T+1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})\leq-\frac{1}{2L}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T+1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})\leq-\frac{1}{2L}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}\leq\frac{2L}{T}\left(f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T+1})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}\leq\frac{2L}{T}\left(f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T+1})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Using the definition of optimality gap from Equation <a href="#A9.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition I.1 (Optimality Gap). ‣ I.1 Basics ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.1</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{t\in[T]}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}\leq\frac{2L}{T}\left(f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{t\in[T]}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}\leq\frac{2L}{T}\left(f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the optimality gap reduces at a rate of <math id="A9.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\frac{1}{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\frac{1}{T})</annotation></semantics></math>, given <math id="A9.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq\frac{1}{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq\frac{1}{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we will give a similar treatment to the gradients derived from zero-order finite differences,</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem I.8</span></span><span id="A9.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Error Bound of Zero-Order Optimization)<span id="A9.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider a
function <math id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> that is <math id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth.
Let the central finite-difference gradient estimator with <math id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> perturbations per iteration, where each perturbation vector <math id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled independently from <math id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and step size <math id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> be</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})}{2\epsilon}\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})}{2\epsilon}\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the expected average squared gradient norm is bounded by</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})}{\eta T\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]}+\frac{Ld\eta^{2}}{2n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})}{\eta T\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]}+\frac{Ld\eta^{2}}{2n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To ensure convergence, the step size must satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta&lt;\frac{2}{L\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta&lt;\frac{2}{L\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This result highlights how the convergence rate depends on the dimension <math id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of perturbations <math id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, and the perturbation magnitude <math id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Specifically, a larger <math id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> or a smaller <math id="A9.Thmtheorem8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> increases the bound, implying slower convergence.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A9.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The central finite-difference gradient estimator for <math id="A9.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> perturbations per iteration is</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})}{2\epsilon}\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}_{i})}{2\epsilon}\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where each <math id="A9.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a perturbation drawn from a Gaussian distribution <math id="A9.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assuming that <math id="A9.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently smooth so that the following Taylor expansions are valid,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E67.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=f(\boldsymbol{w})+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})+O(\epsilon^{2})\text{, and}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>, and</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(\boldsymbol{w})+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})+O(\epsilon^{2})\text{, and}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E68.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=f(\boldsymbol{w})-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})+O(\epsilon^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(\boldsymbol{w})-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})+O(\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Subtracting the above two expansions yields:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})-f(\boldsymbol{w}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}+\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})-f(\boldsymbol{w}-\epsilon\boldsymbol{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E69.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=2\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\epsilon\boldsymbol{v}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging the above result in Equation <a href="#A9.E66" title="In Proof. ‣ I.4 Theorems ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\underbrace{\left((\boldsymbol{v}_{i}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}_{i}+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\right)}_{g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\underbrace{\left((\boldsymbol{v}_{i}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}))\boldsymbol{v}_{i}+\mathcal{O}(\epsilon)\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\right)}_{g(\boldsymbol{v}_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Now we will use the derived </span><math id="A9.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A9.SS4.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in the descent lemma:</span><span id="A9.SS4.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similar to Theorem <a href="#A9.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem I.7 (Error Bound of Backpropagation). ‣ I.4 Theorems ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.7</span></a>, using the Assumption
 <a href="#A9.EGx10" title="Assumption I.2 (Smoothness). ‣ I.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.2</span></a>, we apply the smoothness on <math id="A9.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L}{2}||\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{w}_{t}||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L}{2}||\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{w}_{t}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the gradient descent update with central finite differences, we set the model update rule as</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}=\boldsymbol{w}_{t}-\eta\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}=\boldsymbol{w}_{t}-\eta\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging the model update rule into the smoothness inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation conditioned on <math id="A9.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E74.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})]}_{\text{Term}_{1}}+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}]}_{\text{Term}_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mtext>Term</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></munder><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mtext>Term</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})]}_{\text{Term}_{1}}+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}]}_{\text{Term}_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">Solving <span id="A9.SS4.p7.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Term<sub id="A9.SS4.p7.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">1</sub></span> and <span id="A9.SS4.p7.5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Term<sub id="A9.SS4.p7.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub></span> separately,</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Term<sub id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_sub">1</sub>: </h5>

<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From Lemma <a href="#A9.EGx12" title="Lemma I.3 (Bias of Gradient Estimate of the Central Finite Difference). ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.3</span></a>, we get <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[g(\boldsymbol{v})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[g(\boldsymbol{v})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math>, which also gets us</p>
<table id="A9.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[g(\boldsymbol{v})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[g(\boldsymbol{v})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Term<sub id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>: </h5>

<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The error of <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math> is measured by <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A9.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E75.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})+\delta||^{2}=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+2\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top}\delta+||\delta||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})+\delta||^{2}=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+2\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top}\delta+||\delta||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Taking expectation and noting that <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\delta]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\delta]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[||\delta||^{2}]=\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[||\delta||^{2}]=\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A9.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Using Lemma <a href="#A9.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma I.4 (Variance of Gradient Estimate of the Central Finite Difference). ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.4</span></a> to get the bound of <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A9.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\frac{d+1}{n}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\frac{d}{n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\frac{d+1}{n}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\frac{d}{n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Back to Equation <a href="#A9.E74" title="In Proof. ‣ I.4 Theorems ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">74</span></a>, plugging in Term<sub id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_sub">1</sub> and Term<sub id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.2" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>:</h5>

<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A9.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E78.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\left(\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\frac{d}{n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\left(\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\frac{d}{n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\frac{Ld\eta^{2}}{2n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\frac{Ld\eta^{2}}{2n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Grouping the terms involving <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A9.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E80.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}+\frac{Ld\eta^{2}}{2n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}+\frac{Ld\eta^{2}}{2n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This inequality shows that, provided the step size <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is small enough so that,</p>
<table id="A9.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Summing the inequality over epochs <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A9.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E81.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\eta\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}+\frac{Ld\eta^{2}T}{2n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\eta\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}+\frac{Ld\eta^{2}T}{2n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Rearranging the terms
give us,</p>
<table id="A9.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})}{\eta\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]}+\frac{Ld\eta^{2}T}{2n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})}{\eta\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]}+\frac{Ld\eta^{2}T}{2n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Dividing by <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> gives the bound on the average squared gradient norm:</p>
<table id="A9.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E83.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})}{\eta T\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]}+\frac{Ld\eta^{2}}{2n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})}{\eta T\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]}+\frac{Ld\eta^{2}}{2n}\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">To ensure that
<math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the step size <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> must be chosen so that</p>
<table id="A9.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta&lt;\frac{2}{L\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta&lt;\frac{2}{L\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As the dimension <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> increases (or as the number of samples <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> decreases), the factor</p>
<table id="A9.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">increases. This makes</p>
<table id="A9.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">smaller, which in turn makes the entire bound larger.
In other words, a larger <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> (or a smaller <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>) results in a worse (higher) error bound.
This interplay of <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> also puts limitations on the order of <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, keeping the learning rate quite small for stable learning.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Moving on, we will get the convergence bound of the gradients derived from forward-mode auto differentiation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="156.09" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 156.09" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,156.09) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 150.18 C 0 153.45 2.64 156.09 5.91 156.09 L 471.47 156.09 C 474.73 156.09 477.38 153.45 477.38 150.18 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 150.18 C 1.97 152.36 3.73 154.12 5.91 154.12 L 471.47 154.12 C 473.65 154.12 475.41 152.36 475.41 150.18 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:9.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="128.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 125.84)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The key difference between the two theorems is that the error bound for zero-order optimization includes an additional <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϵ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> term due to the finite-difference approximation, whereas the bound for forward-mode AD is exact and free from such errors.
This makes forward-mode AD theoretically more efficient, as it avoids the additional error introduced by numerical differentiation while maintaining the same dependency on dimension <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and number of perturbations <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem I.9</span></span><span id="A9.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Error Bound of Forward-mode Auto Differentiation)<span id="A9.Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider a
function <math id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> that is <math id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth.
Let the forward-mode AD gradient estimator with <math id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> perturbations per iteration, where each perturbation vector <math id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled independently from <math id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and step size <math id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> be</span></p>
<table id="A9.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(\left(\boldsymbol{v}_{i}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})\right)\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(\left(\boldsymbol{v}_{i}^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})\right)\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the expected average squared gradient norm is bounded by</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E85.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})}{\eta T\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})}{\eta T\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To ensure convergence, the step size must satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta&lt;\frac{2}{L\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta&lt;\frac{2}{L\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This result highlights how the convergence rate depends on the dimension <math id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of perturbations <math id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, and the perturbation magnitude <math id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Specifically, a larger <math id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> or a smaller <math id="A9.Thmtheorem9.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> increases the bound, implying slower convergence.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The forward-mode AD gradient estimator for <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> perturbations per iteration is</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E87.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left((\nabla\boldsymbol{v}_{i}^{\top}f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}))\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left((\nabla\boldsymbol{v}_{i}^{\top}f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}))\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where each <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a perturbation drawn from a Gaussian distribution <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We will use <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> in the descent lemma.
Similar to Theorem <a href="#A9.Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem I.8 (Error Bound of Zero-Order Optimization). ‣ I.4 Theorems ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.8</span></a>, using the Assumption <a href="#A9.EGx10" title="Assumption I.2 (Smoothness). ‣ I.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.2</span></a>, we apply the smoothness on <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E88.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L}{2}||\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{w}_{t}||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L}{2}||\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{w}_{t}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the gradient descent update with forward-mode AD, we set the model update rule as</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}=\boldsymbol{w}_{t}-\eta\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1}=\boldsymbol{w}_{t}-\eta\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging the model update rule into the smoothness inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E90.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation conditioned on <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A9.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E91.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})]}_{\text{Term}_{1}}+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}]}_{\text{Term}_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mtext>Term</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></munder><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mtext>Term</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})]}_{\text{Term}_{1}}+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}]}_{\text{Term}_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">Solving <span id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Term<sub id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">1</sub></span> and <span id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Term<sub id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub></span> separately,</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Term<sub id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px4.1" class="ltx_sub">1</sub>: </h5>

<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From Lemma <a href="#A9.EGx29" title="Lemma I.5 (Bias of Gradient Estimate of Forward-mode Auto Differentiation). ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.5</span></a>, we get <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[g(\boldsymbol{v})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[g(\boldsymbol{v})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math>, which also gets us</p>
<table id="A9.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[g(\boldsymbol{v})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[g(\boldsymbol{v})]=\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Term<sub id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px5.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>: </h5>

<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The error of <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})</annotation></semantics></math> is measured by <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A9.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E92.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})+\delta||^{2}=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+2\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top}\delta+||\delta||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})+\delta||^{2}=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+2\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})^{\top}\delta+||\delta||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Taking expectation and noting that <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\delta]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\delta]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[||\delta||^{2}]=\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[||\delta||^{2}]=\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A9.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Using Lemma <a href="#A9.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma I.6 (Variance of Gradient Estimate of Forward-mode Auto Differentiation). ‣ I.3 Lemmas ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.6</span></a> to get the bound of <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Var}[\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A9.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\frac{d+1}{n}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{v}}[||\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}]=||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}+\frac{d+1}{n}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Back to Equation <a href="#A9.E91" title="In Proof. ‣ Back to Equation , plugging in Term1 and Term2: ‣ I.4 Theorems ‣ Appendix I Proofs of Convergence Bounds ‣ The Cost of Avoiding Backpropagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">91</span></a>, plugging in Term<sub id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.1" class="ltx_sub">1</sub> and Term<sub id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.2" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>:</h5>

<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A9.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E95.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})^{\top}\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A9.E96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}+\frac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Grouping the terms involving <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A9.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E97.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})-\eta\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(97)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This inequality shows that, provided the step size <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is small enough so that,</p>
<table id="A9.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Summing the inequality over epochs <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A9.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E98.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\eta\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\eta\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Rearranging the terms
give us,</p>
<table id="A9.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E99.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})}{\eta\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})}{\eta\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Dividing by <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> gives the bound on the average squared gradient norm:</p>
<table id="A9.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}||\nabla f(\boldsymbol{w}_{t})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E100.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})}{\eta T\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{f(\boldsymbol{w}_{1})-f(\boldsymbol{w}_{T})}{\eta T\left[1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.6" class="ltx_p">To ensure that
<math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the step size <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> must be chosen so that</p>
<table id="A9.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta&lt;\frac{2}{L\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta&lt;\frac{2}{L\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(101)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As the dimension <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> increases (or as the number of samples <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> decreases), the factor</p>
<table id="A9.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p2.2" class="ltx_p">increases. This makes</p>
<table id="A9.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\frac{d+1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p2.3" class="ltx_p">smaller, which in turn makes the entire bound larger.
In other words – similar to zero-order method – a larger <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> (or a smaller <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>) results in a worse (higher) error bound.
This interplay of <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> also puts limitations on the order of <math id="A9.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, keeping the learning rate quite small for stable learning.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
